 "chapter": {
  "number": 18,
  "introduction": null,
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 5,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "pressed -- Or, constrained by the Word. Cf. 2 Corinthians 5:14."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 7,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "Justus -- Titus Justus."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 17,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "cared for -- Contra. John 19:13-16; Acts 24:26,27."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 25,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "instructed -- taught by word of mouth, or, hearsay, i.e. not by revelation. Cf. Galatians 1:11,12.\n\nThe N.T. Scriptures were not then written."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 28,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "that Jesus -- Apollos' ministry seems to have gone no further; Jesus was the long expected Messiah. Of Paul's doctrine of justification through the blood, and sanctification through the Spirit, he seems at that time to have known nothing. See Acts 19:3-6."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
